# The Machine's schedule (beeatlas-ryli), run by supercronic under fly/start.sh. Times
# are in the image's TZ, America/Los_Angeles, which supercronic honors, so these match
# maderas's crontab. Each job's output goes to a dated log under /data/log
# (fly/logged.sh). Their environment is the Machine's: fly.toml's [env] plus the Fly
# secrets other than the API's (fly/start.sh).

# No nightly: since 2026-11-03 it runs on Hostess (ADR 0046,
# docs/runbooks/hostess-nightly.md), which sends its build here and runs
# data/finish-publish.sh over Fly SSH. data/nightly.sh stays in the image for an
# operator to run by hand while the image still carries the pipeline (beeatlas-uibw.7).

# The notes store's hourly snapshot (docs/runbooks/notes-store-dr.md §3), as on
# maderas. Needs NOTES_BACKUP_BUCKET and the AWS key.
0 * * * * /app/fly/logged.sh notes-backup /app/data/.venv/bin/python /app/data/backup_notes.py
